 "_why_not_the_bestiary": "A companion is NOT the bestiary's animal. The bestiary wolf is a 2 HD stat block with its numbers printed flat; a druid's wolf is a Medium body with Str 13 that gains Hit Dice, natural armour and Strength as the druid levels. So its body is written here from the companion section and its numbers are derived (rules/animal_companion.py), never printed.",
